 <315748336+FrontierAIAccountabilityProject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] The anchor sweep: every internal #link resolved against
 the heading that actually exists
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A pass over every markdown link with a fragment, checked against the GitHub/Jekyll
slug of the target file's real headings, found 105 that did not resolve. All are now
pointed at anchors that exist. Three classes:

1. Short-form slugs for long headings — #chunk-3, #chunk-5, #chunk-7, #e26, #e28,
   #e29, #part-i/ii/iii, #g6, #2a, #11, #3, #field-notes, and the companion's
   renamed READ FIRST section — replaced with the full heading slugs, across
   REVIEWERS.md, README.md, MAP.md, LEDGER.md, the record and its eight signposts,
   the queue, the errata register, the packets, filings, research and standards.

2. Anchors for sections that moved — #verify-it and #the-cross-examination now point
   into docs/the_case.md where those sections live; the two front-page #contents
   links point at the merged "Repository structure and contents"; the audit
   directory's #readme points at "The audit directory" inside the record; two
   self-links in docs/questions.md point out to the front page's provenance section
   and the reviewer page's enforcement lane, where the content went.

3. Anchors that never existed — the dossier's #chapter-00 through #chapter-06 (in
   its own index, its seven signpost files, the case, questions, and
   for_legislators) now point at the chapters' actual H1 slugs. The register's
   #e12, #e14, #e15, #e16 and #e30 point at #precision-notes-audit-record: those
   five entries are bold paragraphs inside that section, not headings, so they have
   no anchors of their own. Promoting them to headings would make them linkable
   individually; that edit to the register's structure is left as a decision, not
   made in passing.

The criminal packet's two bad anchors were fixed in its builder, not its output, and
the packet regenerated — which also picked up the OPEN QUESTION 1 status block the
queue gained today, per the rule that packets are regenerated after any edit to
their sources. The register's own link repairs change link targets only; no entry's
text is touched.
